# Trinqa tokens

Source of truth: Home, Portfolio, Earn, Activity. Wallet tab is gone.

- Import `typography`, `spacing`, `radius`, `colors`, `motion` from `@/theme` or `@trinqa/tokens`.
- Visible UI is `@expo/ui/swift-ui`. Do not invent RN layout for these screens.
- Type roles: `pageTitle 30` (tab titles Home/Earn/Activity), `amountHero 32` (defined, unused on Home), `amountDisplay 25`, `amountCurrency 22` (Home total / Earn headline), `sectionTitle 17` (flow header / primary CTA), `kicker 16` (section name), `label 15` (row title, list amount, currency beside 22), `body 14` (supporting sentence), `caption 13`, `footnote 12` (metric label, date), `fine 11` (status), `micro 10` (shortcut).
- Weights: medium / semibold / bold only. RN StyleSheet uses `typeWeightRn` (`500/600/700`). Do not use regular/400.
- Tab chrome is `TabHeader`: left `pageTitle` bold, right 44 profile circle. Profile `Menu` owns Account details + Settings. No support/notification icons. Flow screens keep `ScreenHeader` (back button + `sectionTitle`); the two are not interchangeable.
- One content width per screen: `windowWidth - spacing.screenHorizontal * 2`. Do not give a screen a second gutter by framing a child at a different fixed width.
- Accent budget is 60-30-10: canvas + white surfaces 60, ink + `surfaceLayer` insets 30, and **one** cyan primary per screen for the 10. On Home that one is `Move to grow`; the shortcut row stays neutral.
- Portfolio is not a tab. It is reached by pulling Home past `screenTokens.portfolio.pullRevealThreshold`, plus the `PortfolioPullHint` button for anyone who never finds the gesture. It is a `fullScreenModal`, so the page is replaced and the tab bar goes with it — that swap is what signals the change of mode. The transition is `fade`: the gesture is downward and react-native-screens has no `slide_from_top`.
- Portfolio is built from Home's own parts — `SurfacePanel`, `InsetLayer`, `MetricTile`, `LayeredTransactionRow` — and uses `colors` like every other screen. There is no dark mode anywhere except the welcome screen's local palette.
- On a screen for reading rather than acting, the accent belongs to the data, not to a button. Portfolio's only fill is the split bar; `Change plan` is a white tray tile with a blue label.
- The plan is a setting, not a reading: it lives behind `TabHeader`'s profile menu as `Edit plan`, not on Portfolio. Strategy, risk, time horizon and liquidity are never printed in those words — use the plain-language copy on `PutToWorkRiskProfile` / `PutToWorkHorizon`.
- Money is called `Cash` and `Invested` everywhere, with `banknote.fill` and `lock.fill` beside the labels. Home and Portfolio share one `MetricTile`, so the two cannot drift apart again.
- Portfolio reads top to bottom as: what you have → what we think → what it earned → what changed. The gain sits green beside the total and explains itself in a `Popover`; the commentary is folded into a `DisclosureGroup` so it costs nothing until asked for.
- Transaction status has three states, not two: `Done` / `On its way` / `Didn't go through`, coloured `success` / `pending` / `danger`.
- Home hero: `amountCurrency` + `label` currency; gray `InsetLayer` holds Ready to use / Growing plus Move to grow / Take money out. No hide-balance control. No wallet illustration.
- Home shortcuts: Add money / Pay / More. More is Withdraw + Receive only.
- Status: `colors.success` `#20AD2B`, `colors.danger` `#FF3B30`, `colors.pending` `#787878`. Never use named `'red'`/`'green'`.
- Surfaces: canvas `#F3F3F3`, elevated `surface` `#FFFFFF`, muted `surfaceSecondary` `#F5F5F5`, inset `surfaceLayer` `#F2F2F2`. Do not flatten this by painting buttons with the muted fill. Inset padding is `componentTokens.layer.inset` (4).
- No pure black `#000000`. Ink is `#111111`.
- Accent is iOS systemBlue `#007AFF` (`colors.action*`), the same tint the native tab bar and system links already use. It replaced a cyan that failed contrast against white (2.60) and fought the tab bar for the eye. Do not introduce a second accent hue.
- Do not add new font sizes, hex values, or radii in screens. `walletColors` is leftover illustration palette — do not use it on current screens.
- Native navigation, BottomSheet, and tab motion stay system-owned. Use `motion.press|selection|contentChange|processing` only for micro-motion.
- `motion.press` is `{ duration: 80, releaseDuration: 120, scale: 0.98, opacity: 0.92 }`. Press-in is immediate (80ms ease-out); release settles at 120ms ease-out. No spring, bounce, or layout animation — scale and opacity only, from the element's own centre. Reduce Motion keeps opacity and holds scale at 1. Disabled buttons do not animate.
- Press strength: full scale+opacity on filled CTAs (`PrimaryActionButton`, Home Move to grow / Take money out), tray actions (Portfolio Change plan), and shortcut cards. Opacity only on transaction/list rows and 44pt header circles — scaling a row drags its neighbours. Leave segment pickers, native `Menu`, and `NativeTabs` to the system.
- No haptics on rows. If a haptic is added later, primary CTAs only, light impact.
- Interactive hit boxes are `componentTokens.tapTarget.size` (44). The whole visual control is the target, not the glyph or label inside it. If the visible element is smaller, extend the hit area with padding or frame — do not enlarge the drawing. One control = one action; two affordances on a row get two hit regions. Do not build 44pt header circles with `label` + `systemImage` + `labelStyle('iconOnly')` — SwiftUI keeps the hit on the glyph (~14pt). Use custom-content `HeaderIconButton` (Image inside the circle) so the disc is the target.
- `LayeredInfoBar` is trailing-only when it has an action. The leading status (`Done` / `On its way` / `Didn't go through`) is information, not a control. The row body is a separate hit if the card itself is tappable.
- Every interactive element needs `accessibilityLabel`. Add `accessibilityHint` when the outcome is not obvious from the label.
